IMPORT prelude

-- The dinner race: the ledgers every fixture in this directory keeps, and
-- the brief's properties P1 to P6 as boolean decisions over them
-- (REGULATIVE-LOWERING-SPEC.md section 5.1).
--
-- The fixtures d1-naive.l4, d2-reread.l4 and d3-atomic.l4 IMPORT this
-- file, so a property here is evaluated on the same types the contract
-- writes. Each of the brief's six variables lives in one ledger cell:
--
--   brief variable  ledger cell                                   read by
--   ledger          OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`             RECALL ALL
--   dinners         OFFICIAL's `dinners bought`, less             RECALL ALL
--                   OFFICIAL's `dinners cancelled`
--   okAtBuy         OFFICIAL's `open at acceptance`               RECALL ALL
--   belief          Alice's `belief`  (NOTHING is Unknown)        RECALL
--   alice           Alice's `plan`    (NOTHING is Planning)       RECALL
--   message         Messages's `message` (NOTHING is None)        RECALL
--
-- The dinner ledger's own records are COMMITs, to the official record,
-- because they bind every party; what Alice knows and where she is are
-- RECORDs in her own ledger, and the message's progress is a RECORD in
-- the ledger of Messages.
--
-- Every input of a property below is named for the cell it reads: a LIST
-- input takes that cell's RECALL ALL, a MAYBE input takes its RECALL (the
-- latest entry). A cell read only by RECALL is single-valued: its history
-- is not part of the brief's state, and an explorer that kept it would
-- split the brief's states (README.md, "What the explorer must know").
--
-- No rule here reads a ledger itself. A rule with no inputs is evaluated
-- once and its value kept, so one that did RECALL would answer every
-- later question with the record as it stood the first time it was asked
-- (README.md, "Traps").

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    World      -- the one party that acts (option C): each act names its actor
    Alice      -- whose own ledger holds what she believes and where she is
    Messages   -- whose own ledger holds the message "I bought it"

-- What the dinner ledger has recorded: the arrangement opened with dinner
-- unbought, and then, perhaps, Bob's purchase took it.
DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    opened
    taken

-- Where Alice is: planning to buy, has checked, is re-reading (D2 only),
-- has bought, has stopped.
DECLARE Plan IS ONE OF
    planning
    checked
    reading
    bought
    stopped

-- The message "I bought it", from Bob to Alice.
DECLARE `Message state` IS ONE OF
    `in transit`
    delivered

DECLARE Dinner IS ONE OF
    `dinner for two`

§ `Reading the ledgers`

GIVEN `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A Status
`the ledger's status` MEANS
    IF elem taken `dinner status record` THEN taken ELSE opened

GIVEN `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the ledger is open` MEANS `the ledger's status` `dinner status record` EQUALS opened

GIVEN `dinners bought`    IS A LIST OF Dinner
      `dinners cancelled` IS A LIST OF Dinner
GIVETH A NUMBER
`dinners` MEANS count `dinners bought` - count `dinners cancelled`

GIVEN plan IS A MAYBE Plan
GIVETH A Plan
`where Alice is` MEANS fromMaybe planning plan

§ `The properties`

-- P1, safety (always): a dinner is bought only if the ledger's record said
-- open at the instant the purchase took effect. The fixtures COMMIT one
-- `open at acceptance` per purchase, at the moment it takes effect.
GIVEN `open at acceptance` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every dinner was accepted while open` MEANS all (GIVEN ok YIELD ok) `open at acceptance`

-- P2, safety (always): Alice buys at most one dinner.
GIVEN `dinners bought`    IS A LIST OF Dinner
      `dinners cancelled` IS A LIST OF Dinner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`at most one dinner is bought` MEANS `dinners` `dinners bought` `dinners cancelled` <= 1

-- P3, reachability (some reachable state): Alice believes dinner is still
-- open after Bob's purchase has taken it. A reachable state is the expected
-- answer.
GIVEN belief                 IS A MAYBE Status
      `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Alice's belief is stale` MEANS
    belief EQUALS JUST opened AND `the ledger's status` `dinner status record` EQUALS taken

-- P4, safety over steps: once one dinner is bought, it stays bought. This
-- is the state label; the property is that no step goes from a state where
-- it holds to one where it does not.
GIVEN `dinners bought`    IS A LIST OF Dinner
      `dinners cancelled` IS A LIST OF Dinner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`one dinner is bought` MEANS `dinners` `dinners bought` `dinners cancelled` EQUALS 1

-- P5, liveness (eventually): Alice buys or stops. Liveness needs a model
-- checker and a fairness assumption (spec section 5.3); this is the label.
GIVEN plan IS A MAYBE Plan
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Alice has bought or stopped` MEANS
    `where Alice is` plan EQUALS bought OR `where Alice is` plan EQUALS stopped

-- P6, liveness: if the ledger stays open (Bob never buys), Alice eventually
-- buys: always `the ledger is open` implies eventually `one dinner is
-- bought`. Both labels are above.

-- The non-vacuity control of spec section 6.3: under every fairness
-- assumption used, "eventually Bob has bought" must be VIOLATED, or P6 has
-- passed on an empty set of runs.
GIVEN `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Bob has bought` MEANS NOT (`the ledger is open` `dinner status record`)

§ `The properties on ledgers written out by hand`

-- The initial state: the arrangement has opened, nothing else is recorded.
#ASSERT `every dinner was accepted while open` EMPTY
#ASSERT `at most one dinner is bought` EMPTY EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT (`Alice's belief is stale` NOTHING (LIST opened))
#ASSERT NOT (`one dinner is bought` EMPTY EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT (`Alice has bought or stopped` NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the ledger is open` (LIST opened)

-- Sequence A under D1: Alice checked while open, Bob's purchase was
-- recorded, and Alice's purchase took effect after it.
#ASSERT NOT (`every dinner was accepted while open` (LIST FALSE))
#ASSERT `Alice's belief is stale` (JUST opened) (LIST opened, taken)
#ASSERT `Bob has bought` (LIST opened, taken)

-- Sequence B: Alice's purchase took effect before Bob's.
#ASSERT `every dinner was accepted while open` (LIST TRUE)
#ASSERT `one dinner is bought` (LIST `dinner for two`) EMPTY
#ASSERT `Alice has bought or stopped` (JUST bought)

-- The mutants: a cancelled dinner, and a purchase recorded twice.
#ASSERT NOT (`one dinner is bought` (LIST `dinner for two`) (LIST `dinner for two`))
#ASSERT NOT (`at most one dinner is bought` (LIST `dinner for two`, `dinner for two`) EMPTY)
